  "title": "Mahatma Gandhi",
  "summary": "Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi (1869–1948), called Mahatma, was born in Porbandar in western India. Working in South Africa from 1893, he developed satyagraha, a method of non-violent resistance, and later led India’s independence movement, including the Non-Cooperation campaign and mass civil disobedience against British law such as the Salt March of 1930. He was assassinated on 30 January 1948. His methods inspired non-violent civil rights movements worldwide.",
